    {
      "type": "stage",
      "kicker": "What it is",
      "narration": "So what is blood pressure? It is the force of blood pushing against the walls of your arteries. Let's look inside one. With every heartbeat, blood surges in and presses outward on the wall. The elastic wall stretches, then springs back. We measure this pressure in millimetres of mercury.",
