          }
        },
        {
          "say": [
            "millimetres"
          ],
          "note": "Measured in millimetres of mercury (mmHg)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "kicker": "The pressure wave",
      "narration": "Now watch one heartbeat. The heart contracts, and a pressure wave travels along the artery. The pressure peaks: this is the systolic pressure. Then the heart rests, and the pressure falls to its lowest: the diastolic pressure. [pause] Together, these two values make your reading.",
