    {
      "type": "stage",
      "kicker": "What's normal",
      "narration": "For most adults, 90 over 60 or lower is low. The ideal range is between 90 over 60 and 120 over 80. Between 120 over 80 and 140 over 90, you're at risk. And 140 over 90 or higher is high blood pressure, called hypertension. [pause] It is diagnosed when readings are that high on two different days.",
