    {
      "type": "stage",
      "kicker": "The damage",
      "narration": "Year after year, high pressure strains the arteries and damages their walls. In the heart, that can mean a heart attack. In the brain, a stroke. In the kidneys, kidney damage. [pause] And a heart forced to pump harder can eventually fail: that is heart failure.",
